# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# The deploy was uploading ~410 MB and spending about six minutes on the upload
# alone, which is the difference between a two-minute fix and a coffee break if
# we need to ship under time pressure. Nothing here is reachable from the app.
#
# ── The rule for adding to this file ──────────────────────────────────────
# The Vercel build runs exactly one command — `npx expo export --platform web`
# (see vercel.json; there is no postinstall and no prepare). So the only files
# that must survive are the ones METRO resolves. Metro resolves `require()` at
# BUILD time, and a require with no file on disk is a build error, not a
# fallback — so an over-eager entry here breaks the deploy rather than degrading
# it. Before adding a path, check it has no `require()` reaching into it:
#
#     grep -rn "assets/collectee/<dir>" src | grep require
#
# Most of assets/ genuinely ships and must NOT be listed. `display/` alone has
# 376 require() sites; `models/`, `depth/`, `items/`, `subjects/`, `avatars/`,
# `backdrops/`, `communities/` and `brand/` are all wired into registries too.

# Raw hand-off blobs from the HuggingFace/TRELLIS bakes — source GLBs and the
# stills they were baked from. 104 MB, and nothing in src/ or scripts/ reads it.
exports/

# Bake INPUTS. Referenced only by scripts/verified-weapon-manifest.ts, which is
# reached solely by the bake:* and validate:weapons scripts — none of which run
# on Vercel. The baked OUTPUTS live in assets/collectee/models and do ship.
assets/collectee/trellis-inputs/

# Reference imagery handed to the art agent. Zero references anywhere in the
# repo, and third-party material we deliberately do not publish (§15).
assets/collectee/character-references/

# Local working files. Already gitignored, listed so a CLI deploy from a dirty
# tree cannot sweep them up.
scratchpad/

# Motion handoff pack for the animator. 64 MB of screenshots, brand art and a
# PDF; nothing in src/ requires any of it, so uploading it to every deploy
# would undo the saving this file exists for.
animation/
